{"title":"Longest Common Substring","difficulty":"Medium","statement":"You are given two strings `s1` and `s2`. A **substring** is a contiguous block of characters. Find the length of the longest string that appears as a substring of both `s1` and `s2`.\n\nThe interviewer first asked a warm-up: the length of the longest common **prefix** of the two strings. The real question is the longest common **substring**, which may start at any position in either string.\n\nPrint the length of that longest common substring (0 if the strings share no character).","inputFormat":"The first line contains the string `s1`.\nThe second line contains the string `s2`.","outputFormat":"Print a single integer: the length of the longest common substring.","constraints":["1 ≤ |s1|, |s2| ≤ 1000","`s1` and `s2` consist of lowercase English letters"],"examples":[{"input":"abcdxyz\nxyzabcd","output":"4","explanation":"The substring `abcd` appears in both strings. `xyz` has only length 3, so the answer is 4."},{"input":"zxabcdezy\nyzabcdezx","output":"6","explanation":"`abcdez` occurs in both strings and no longer block is shared."},{"input":"abc\ndef","output":"0","explanation":"The strings have no character in common."}],"tests":[{"input":"a\na","output":"1"},{"input":"a\nb","output":"0"},{"input":"abc\nabc","output":"3"},{"input":"abcdef\nxyz","output":"0"},{"input":"zzzz\nzz","output":"2"},{"input":"abab\nbaba","output":"3"},{"input":"abcde\ncdeab","output":"3"},{"input":"ba\nab","output":"1"},{"input":"gch\ncr","output":"1"},{"input":"aa\na","output":"1"},{"input":"ac\nbbb","output":"0"},{"input":"yv\nwxck","output":"0"},{"input":"aaab\nbbab","output":"2"},{"input":"aab\nac","output":"1"},{"input":"mw\narxm","output":"1"},{"input":"baabbaabb\nbbbbaa","output":"4"},{"input":"a\naacccccab","output":"1"},{"input":"bdu\nfoqypsfjawv","output":"0"},{"input":"\","output":"1000"},{"input":"\","output":"500"},{"input":"\","output":"17"},{"input":"\","output":"4"}],"complexity":{"time":"O(|s1| · |s2